  "_comment": [
    "Coarse semantic types used by the selectional-restriction checker.",
    "'anchors' maps each coarse type to WordNet synsets; a noun sense belongs",
    "to the type when one of these synsets appears in the sense's hypernym",
    "closure. 'fallback' assigns the same types by lemma, so the system still",
    "runs (and the tests stay hermetic) when WordNet is not installed.",
    "Anchors were chosen against actual WordNet hypernym paths, not intuition: book.n.01 sits under publication.n.01 > artifact.n.01 and never under communication.n.02, so 'communication' needs several anchors to cover the written-work senses."
